    "['ipv6 enable', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols router-advertisement interface all', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nset protocols router-advertisement interface all\\n##\\n\\nAlternatively, if you specifically want IPv6 enabled on an interface without router advertisements (closer to the Cisco `ipv6 enable` behavior):\\n\\n##\\nset interfaces <interface-name> family inet6\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Juniper, enabling IPv6 on an interface is typically done by adding `family inet6` to the interface configuration, which is more fundamental than Cisco's `ipv6 enable`. The first option with router-advertisement is provided because Cisco's `ipv6 enable` often implicitly enables IPv6 ND/RA.\", 'trans_template': 'set protocols router-advertisement interface all'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set interfaces <interface-name> family inet6', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nset protocols router-advertisement interface all\\n##\\n\\nAlternatively, if you specifically want IPv6 enabled on an interface without router advertisements (closer to the Cisco `ipv6 enable` behavior):\\n\\n##\\nset interfaces <interface-name> family inet6\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Juniper, enabling IPv6 on an interface is typically done by adding `family inet6` to the interface configuration, which is more fundamental than Cisco's `ipv6 enable`. The first option with router-advertisement is provided because Cisco's `ipv6 enable` often implicitly enables IPv6 ND/RA.\", 'trans_template': 'set interfaces <interface-name> family inet6'}]]": 1,
    "['ipv6 address [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family inet6 address 2001:db8:3::1/64', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the Juniper equivalent of the Cisco `ipv6 address` command:\\n\\n##\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family inet6 address 2001:db8:3::1/64\\n##\\n\\nThis command:\\n1. Selects the GigabitEthernet1/0/0 interface (ge-1/0/0 in Juniper)\\n2. Sets the IPv6 address (family inet6)\\n3. Assigns the same address and prefix length (2001:db8:3::1/64)\\n4. Uses unit 0 which is Juniper's equivalent of the main interface context\", 'trans_template': 'set interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family inet6 address 2001:db8:3::1/64'}]]": 1,
    "['ipv6 router [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols isis interface ge-1/0/0', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nset protocols isis interface ge-1/0/0\\nset protocols isis interface ge-1/0/4\\n##', 'trans_template': 'set protocols isis interface ge-1/0/0'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols isis interface ge-1/0/4', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nset protocols isis interface ge-1/0/0\\nset protocols isis interface ge-1/0/4\\n##', 'trans_template': 'set protocols isis interface ge-1/0/4'}]]": 2,
    "['ipv6 enable', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family inet6', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family inet6\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/4 unit 0 family inet6\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n1. In Juniper, enabling IPv6 on an interface is done by configuring the `inet6` family under the interface unit.\\n2. The command is applied to both GigabitEthernet interfaces (ge-1/0/0 and ge-1/0/4) to match the Cisco configuration.\\n3. Juniper requires specifying the unit number (typically 0) when configuring interfaces.', 'trans_template': 'set interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family inet6'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set interfaces ge-1/0/4 unit 0 family inet6', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family inet6\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/4 unit 0 family inet6\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n1. In Juniper, enabling IPv6 on an interface is done by configuring the `inet6` family under the interface unit.\\n2. The command is applied to both GigabitEthernet interfaces (ge-1/0/0 and ge-1/0/4) to match the Cisco configuration.\\n3. Juniper requires specifying the unit number (typically 0) when configuring interfaces.', 'trans_template': 'set interfaces ge-1/0/4 unit 0 family inet6'}]]": 1,
